---
import "../styles/global.css";
import site from "../data/site.json";

const heroStyle = "background-image: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(12,45,47,.92), rgba(12,45,47,.42)), url('/images/wccl/img_2832.jpg')";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <meta name="description" content="The field experience and rehabilitation expertise behind WCCL Systems." />
    <title>Experience | WCCL Systems</title>
    <style>
      .detail-hero { min-height:55vh; display:grid; align-items:end; padding:8rem 0 4rem; color:#fff; background-color:#0c2d2f; background-position:center; background-size:cover; }
      .detail-body { max-width:850px; padding:5rem 1.5rem 6rem; }
      .detail-body p { font-size:1.2rem; line-height:1.75; color:#385355; }
      .detail-body h2 { font-size:2rem; color:#16494a; margin-top:2.5rem; }
      .experience-list { margin:1.5rem 0 2.5rem; padding-left:1.25rem; }
      .experience-list li { margin:.8rem 0; color:#385355; font-size:1.08rem; line-height:1.6; }
      .detail-link { display:inline-block; margin-top:2rem; padding:.9rem 1.2rem; background:#16494a; color:#fff; text-decoration:none; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <section class="detail-hero" style={heroStyle}>
        <div class="container">
          <a class="text-link light" href="/">← Back to WCCL Systems</a>
          <p class="eyebrow light">Experience</p>
          <h1>{site.intro.headline}</h1>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="container detail-body">
        <p>{site.intro.paragraphs[0]}</p>
        <p>{site.intro.paragraphs[1]}</p>

        <h2>Built from field experience</h2>
        <p>Marc Valdes began working in the field as a sewer concrete installer in the 1980s. That hands-on work revealed the persistent challenges facing sewer and wastewater infrastructure throughout the Pacific Northwest: infiltration, deteriorated concrete, difficult groundwater conditions, and too few dependable repair options.</p>
        <p>In 1996, Marc founded WCCL Systems to deliver a higher standard of construction and rehabilitation for sanitary sewer infrastructure. The company was built around rigorous quality control, practical problem-solving, innovative repair methods, and responsive customer service.</p>

        <h2>Specialized rehabilitation expertise</h2>
        <p>For nearly three decades, WCCL Systems has developed solutions for demanding rehabilitation work at wastewater treatment facilities and other critical infrastructure sites. Our experience includes lining, waterproofing, structural repair, coatings, inspections, and specialized injection work for structures exposed to hydrogen sulfide (H₂S), high groundwater, abrasion, and chemical attack.</p>
        <p>Marc’s dedication to quality workmanship, dependable solutions, and exceptional customer service has helped establish WCCL Systems as a leading concrete rehabilitation contractor in the Pacific Northwest. Having installed about 1,000,000 square feet of Raven 405, Marc continues to build on that legacy, with a commitment to delivering millions of additional square feet of rehabilitation over the next decade.</p>
        <p>WCCL Systems is a certified applicator of Duraplate, Warren Environmental, and other industrial coating products.</p>
        <ul class="experience-list">
          <li>About 1,000,000 square feet of Raven 405 installed in concrete rehabilitation applications.</li>
          <li>Collaboration with waterproofing manufacturers and suppliers to develop practical injection and coating solutions.</li>
          <li>Field-tested work to stop leaks, protect concrete, and extend the service life of utility and wastewater structures.</li>
          <li>Direct support for municipalities, utilities, engineers, industrial facilities, and contractors throughout the region.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>A continuing family commitment</h2>
        <p>Today, Marc works alongside his son, Andrew Valdes, combining decades of construction experience with emerging technologies and personal, hands-on customer service. Together, they continue to help infrastructure owners protect critical assets with dependable solutions and accountable execution.</p>
        <a class="detail-link" href="/#contact">Discuss your project →</a>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
